BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The 28th Annual Family & Friends Golf Tournament
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260913T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260913T200000
UID:66dcf7ffbdfc04fc8c0c3fec95ab74f8@jccc.on.ca
DESCRIPTION:The 28th Annual Family & Friends Golf Tournament will be held 
 on Sunday September 13\, 2026\, on the Classic Course at Rolling Hills Gol
 f Club in Stouffville. This day is also National Grandparents’ Day\, so 
 we will have special prizes for the Grandparent/Grandchild Champions! This
  is a chance for families and friends to share a fun day of golf – all s
 kill levels are welcome and there are lots of prizes to be won! After a gr
 eat day of golfing\, there will be games\, a raffle\, prize presentations 
 and dinner back at the JCCC. We encourage everyone to join with grandparen
 ts\, grandchildren\, parents\, siblings\, aunts\, uncles\, cousins\, or ju
 st as a group of friends. There will be awards for 3 categories: iA Privat
 e Wealth Cup (Lowest Scramble Score for foursome) Consul General Cup (Lowe
 st Family* Scramble) * Must all be related Roy & Kay Shin Memorial Cup (Lo
 west Grandparent/Grandchild Score) Note: a foursome cannot win more than 1
  category. As in the past\, it will be an early Shotgun format (8:30am sta
 rt for everyone) and the format is a Texas Scramble (where everyone hits a
  tee shot\, then the foursome picks the best lie\, and everyone else plays
  their ball from that spot\, and so on). We are so appreciative of iA Priv
 ate Wealth's Marty Kobayashi\, confirmed again this year as our Platinum S
 ponsor. So please come on out for a fun day!! The Tournament is limited to
  the first 144 golfers registered. We had an overwhelming response last ye
 ar so make sure to get your registration submitted before it fills up. REG
 ISTRATION NEW THIS YEAR: Registration will ONLY be on-line through the "Re
 gister" link below. You must register the whole team (4 players) at sign u
 p. See below for the details. The registration link will open on Monday Ju
 ly 13\, 2026 at 10 AM . Register Please note that Green Fees\, Cart Rental
  fees and food prices have all gone up substantially over the past year\, 
 so we have no choice but to increase entry fees. However\, we have elimina
 ted the 2-price system so now all golfers pay the same price: Entry Fee: R
 egular 4 player team ($145 pp - includes tax) OR Gold Sponsor 4 player tea
 m $680. Fees include – Green fees/Shared Power Cart/Musubi Lunch/Awards/
 Dinner/Prizes. Dinners only: Adults $35 (includes tax) / Children (under 1
 0 years $12 (includes tax)). More Registration details: Register as 4 pers
 on Teams – Regular Fee or as Gold Sponsor Register up to 2 teams in one 
 application. Award categories and extra dinners are included in the regist
 ration form. Main contact/payee required to sign up by name\, additional p
 layers can be left anonymous. Substitute players allowed\, no refunds. Con
 tact the organizers to confirm all player names no later than Monday Augus
 t 31st . Other sponsorship types: In Memoriam ($200) / Bronze level ($200)
  which include signage and 2 adults dinners – please contact the organiz
 ers to provide more details. For ALL inquiries/questions : Organizers Shar
 on Marubashi by e-mail \, or cell (647-291-4751) and Dawna Kobayashi by e-
 mail \, or cell (416-407-8102).\n\nCategories: Community Event
